  body: "# Industrial accident question and a benefit claim\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe chapter distinguishes
    an identifiable accident arising out of and in the course of employed-earner employment, with territorial limits,
    from the later personal-injury and benefit questions.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nRead the full conditions
    in DMG 66001 and the qualification in 66002; the project does not decide whether an accident occurred. The “accident
    is the injury” case type has separate guidance in 69022. From 5 December 2012 the source restricts applications
    for declarations without an IA claim.\n\n## Inspected passages\n\n- [DMG 66001, PDF page 7](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a814e8b40f0b6230269697f/dmgch66.pdf#page=7).\n\
    - [DMG 66002, PDF page 7](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a814e8b40f0b6230269697f/dmgch66.pdf#page=7).\n\
    - [DMG 66008, PDF page 7](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a814e8b40f0b6230269697f/dmgch66.pdf#page=7).\n\
    - [DMG 69022, PDF page 6](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6172830bd3bf7f55f94795f8/dmgch69.pdf#page=6).\n\
    \n## Additional context\n\n- [Context: chapter 66, PDF page 8](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a814e8b40f0b6230269697f/dmgch66.pdf#page=8).\n\
    \n## Evidence and review status\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of captured DWP guidance, not an
    official DWP document. Definitions and semantic associations are model-assisted proposals awaiting specialist
    review. No individual entitlement decision, medical conclusion, award calculation or executable rule is provided.\n\
    \nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, legal event and claimant-event dates are separate.
    Current legal applicability is unresolved. Page numbers are one-based PDF positions; machine extraction may
    damage reading order, characters and footnotes. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n- `dmg-vol11-ch66`:
    PDF `8a2f49feb6557c0bc2833c308c458204e0f28cefeabbe85bc7a1ec3ae0461155`; extracted pages `a4efac777c187bd7b7d95994b53893fc4b480fe08736216f641a27ec9d6ed3d7`;
    acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:34.019999Z`.\n- `dmg-vol11-ch69`: PDF `3bbd376d12fc0a6633010680e88d11efdf7f5b34dde311016a073e80ac3e56b8`;
    extracted pages `fcaf30907d52d71cc7473cf40c8c876469efc3f8d18f7f9af7b3d32bf5016d95`; acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:34.033473Z`.\n"
  resource: https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a814e8b40f0b6230269697f/dmgch66.pdf#page=7
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/industrial-accident-employment
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: Both arising out of and in the course of employed-earner employment are expressly required.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol11-ch66/0059
      quote: "66301   Before accepting an accident as an IA the DM must be satisfied that it arose\n\n        1.\
        \      out of and\n\n        2.      in the course of\n\n        the injured person’s employed earner’s
        employment1 (see DMG 66061 et seq).\n                                                                  \
        \           1 SS Act 98, s 29(6)(b)"
      locator: DMG 66301
  - target: term/industrial-unrecorded-accident-evidence
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source provides evidence guidance for unreported or unwitnessed accidents.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol11-ch66/0010
      quote: "66045   When considering an unreported or unwitnessed accident the DM should note that\n\n       \
        \ 1.    if notice of an accident is given and recorded by the employer soon after it\n              happened
        this is usually enough to prove a claim that there was an accident\n\n        2.    the absence of a record
        does not mean that the claim cannot succeed but\n              any long delay in reporting an accident may
        throw doubt on the claim and\n              should be carefully investigated\n\n        3.    corroboration
        by witnesses is helpful in cases where there is doubt over\n              whether an accident occurred."
      locator: DMG 66045
  - target: term/iidb-loss-of-faculty
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: IIDB requires the further injury/loss-of-faculty chain; an accident declaration is not the
      complete award.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol11-ch69/0002
      quote: "69002 To obtain IIDB there must be personal injury from an accident or the contraction of a PD resulting\n\
        in loss of physical or mental faculty which results in disability and disablement.\n\n\n\nMeaning of terms"
      locator: DMG 69002
